 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Spreadsheets solve everyday problems: class marks and averages, a shopping list with costs, a budget, sales records, a timetable.\nSteps:\n1. Type headings (labels) in the first row: Item, Quantity, Unit price, Total.\n2. Enter the data.\n3. Enter a formula in the first Total cell, for example =B{2}*C{2}.\n4. Copy (fill) the formula down: it changes automatically to =B{3}*C{3}, =B{4}*C{4} (relative references).\n5. Use =SUM(D{2}:D{6}) for the grand total.\n6. Format the cells (currency FCFA, bold headings), sort the data, and make a chart (column, bar, pie, line).\nWhen data changes, the results update automatically.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "q": 4,
   "p": 250
  },
  "problem": "In a shopping sheet, B{2} (quantity) is {q} and C{2} (unit price) is {p} FCFA. What formula goes in D{2}, and what is the total?",
  "steps": [
   "Total = quantity × unit price, so D{2} has =B{2}*C{2}.",
   "{q} × {p} = {q * p} FCFA."
  ],
  "answer": "=B{2}*C{2}, giving {q * p} FCFA.",
  "checks": []
 },
